@@ -1221,6 +1222,25 @@ def my_callback(session_id: str, kind: str, reason: str, **kwargs):
 
 **Use cases:** Re-inject session context after compaction, refresh an external index, count compactions.
 
+### `on_user_rule_extracted`
+
+Fires after the background rule extractor (`compression.rule_extractor_routes`) kept one or more items whose scope is the project rather than the chat: a rule, fact or decision the user stated that holds in other chats too. Every item's quote was checked to be an exact substring of a message the user wrote. It runs in the extractor's thread, after the turn was delivered, never ahead of a user turn.
+
+**Callback signature:**
+
+```python
+def my_callback(session_id: str, items: list[dict], **kwargs) -> str | None:
+```
+
+| Parameter | Type | Description |
+|-----------|------|-------------|
+| `session_id` | `str` | The session whose user said it. |
+| `items` | `list[dict]` | Each with `kind` (`rule`, `fact` or `decision`), `quote` (the user's exact words), `id` (its decision-ledger id), and `at` (the day) and `msg` (the message id) when known. |
+
+**Return value:** a `str` is a one-shot note for the session's next turn (added to the user's message, like a gateway note), for example to say what was saved and how to undo it. Other returns are ignored. Callbacks are not timeout-bounded.
+
+**Use cases:** Save project facts to a project memory automatically, mirror rules to an external store.
+
 ### `post_curator_run`
 
 Fires once after a curator pass has written its per-run report directory, so a plugin or shell hook can react to what the curator changed (route new skills to another profile, override an archival, write an audit log) instead of polling `logs/curator/`.
